<item>
            <title>[LU-20433] lfs find ! -m &lt;idx&gt; is inverted</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20433</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-16622&quot; title=&quot;allow &amp;quot;lfs find --ost&amp;quot; to accept an OST range&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-16622&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-16622&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; unified the lfs find -m/-i/-O handling and dropped param.fp_exclude_mdt = !!neg_opt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;fp_exclude_mdt is now never set in lfs.c (only fp_exclude_obd), but the MDT matcher still reads it (liblustreapi_pfind.c:724/727).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So ! -m &amp;lt;idx&amp;gt; loses its negation and behaves like -m &amp;lt;idx&amp;gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;-i/-O (OST) are unaffected.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reproduction (DNE, 2 MDTs):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
### lfs find -m 0 &#160; (control: files ON MDT0)
.
./dir_on_mdt0
./dir_on_mdt0/f0

### lfs find ! -m 0 &#160;(should list files NOT on MDT0 = dir_on_mdt1/f1)
.
./dir_on_mdt0
./dir_on_mdt0/f0

### lfs find -m 1 &#160; &#160;(control: files ON MDT1 -&amp;gt; expect dir_on_mdt1, f1)
./dir_on_mdt1
./dir_on_mdt1/f1

### lfs find ! -m 1 &#160;(should be files NOT on MDT1 -&amp;gt; expect $D, dir_on_mdt0, f0)
./dir_on_mdt1
./dir_on_mdt1/f1&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;found by commit-hunter-v1&lt;/p&gt;</description>
